    E1[Event E1<br/>type: order.created<br/>key: order-123]:::event
    R1[Resolve order.created<br/>then evaluate active revision]:::rule
    Decision[Decision]:::rule
    Tx[(One transaction:<br/>inbox + execution + outbox)]:::durable
    Same[New event E2<br/>type: payment.requested<br/>key: order-123]:::target
    Different[New event E3<br/>type: customer.notification<br/>key: customer-55]:::target
    Router[Route each new event by its own<br/>type and partition key]:::target
    R2[Payment rule set]:::rule
    R3[Notification rule set]:::rule

    E1 --> R1 --> Decision --> Tx
    Tx -. proposed: emit-event action .-> Same
    Tx -. proposed: emit-event action .-> Different
    Same --> Router --> R2
    Different --> Router --> R3
    Note[Rule chaining chooses the next event type.<br/>Partition routing independently chooses its key and worker/shard.<br/>The current runtime persists effects; first-class next-event envelopes are proposed.]:::target
